error[NK2308]: Every line `io::lines()` reads is gathered here, each a view of a buffer of the stream's pool, and their number grows with the input.
  --> tests/all_lines_gathered_at_once_are_refused.nika:9:5
   |
 9 |     let all: Vec[String] = io::lines().collect()
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A stream reads into a fixed pool of buffers, sized by the places that hold a view of its items from one turn to the next; a list of all its items would need a new buffer for every one.
   = help: Gather copies with `.cloned()` before `.collect()`, process each line in a `for` over `io::lines()`, or hand the lines to a task over a bounded channel.
